# A generic Yo fn whose binder sits under a pointer (`a : *U`) called with the
# CALLER's unresolved binder (`*T`) left `U` unbound in the caller's
# definition-time trial, so a callee result that mentions `U` (`-> *U`,
# `-> Pair(*U, *U)`) failed the trial with a swallowed E0613 "Cannot infer the
# type parameter"
# (issues/fixed/a-generic-fn-with-a-nested-binder-fails-its-generic-callers-trial.md).
# The trial failure is swallowed, so the only observable is YO_DEBUG_SWALLOW: the
# golden pins that no swallowed error points into main.yo, and that main.yo checks.
env=YO_DEBUG_SWALLOW=1
stdout_keep_match=--> main\.yo:[0-9]+:[0-9]+|check: main\.yo — evaluator OK
timeout=120
